1. What is an Array?
An Array is a container object that holds a fixed number of a single data type. Arrays are zero-indexed,
meaning the first element is at index 0.

2. Declaring an Array
dataType [] arrayName;
dataType arrayName[];//not preferred
int [] numbers; //Declares array of integers
String [] names; //Declares array of String

