Since arrays in Java are not objects (they are considered primitives types), they do not have built in methods for operations
like sorting or searching. The Arrays class is a utility class that contains static methods to perform various operations on arrays
Sorting:Arrays.sort()
Searching:Arrays.binarySearch()
Filling:Arrays.fill()
Equality Check:Arrays.equals()
Copying: Arrays.copyOf()

