12. Copy array with copyOfRange method
public static int [] copyOfRange(int [] original, int from , int to)
original: the original array you want to copy from
from : the starting index (inclusive) of the range to copy
to: the ending index (exclusive) of the range to copy

int[] originalArray = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70};

// Copy elements from index 2 to 5 (exclusive)
int[] copiedArray = Arrays.copyOfRange(originalArray, 2, 5);
// Print the copied array
System.out.println(Arrays.toString(copiedArray));  // Output: [30, 40, 50]

