14. Sorting an array
You do not need to write your own sorting logic,  you can use Arrays.sort()

int[] nums = {3, 1, 4, 5, 2};
Arrays.sort(nums); // Sort the array in ascending order
System.out.println(Arrays.toString(nums)); // Output: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

For descending order, you can use a custom comparator (although you need to convert the array to a Integer[] object since
primitive types like int [] do not support comparators)

Integer[] nums = {50, 30, 10, 40, 20};  // Use Integer, not int
Arrays.sort(nums, Collections.reverseOrder());  // Sorts in descending order
System.out.println("Sorted Array (Descending): " + Arrays.toString(nums));
Sorted Array (Descending): [50, 40, 30, 20, 10]

15. Reversing an Array
You can reverse an array by swapping elements from start and end

public static void reverse(int[] arr) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = arr.length - 1;
        while (left < right) {
            // Swap the elements
            int temp = arr[left];
            arr[left] = arr[right];
            arr[right] = temp;
            left++;
            right--;
        }
    }

16. Searching for an element in an array
You can search for an element using a simple linear search or a binary search (if the array is sorted)
public static int linearSearch(int[] arr, int key) {
        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
            if (arr[i] == key) {
                return i;  // Return index if found
            }
        }
        return -1;  // Return -1 if element not found
    }
//using binarySearch as array is sorted
int[] nums = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
int key = 30;
int result = Arrays.binarySearch(nums, key);  // Uses binary search

Linear Search : O(n)
Binary Search: O(log n)
Sorting: O(n log n) //merge sort, quick sort or heap sort

sorting+binary search: O(n log n)+O(log n)=O(n log n)

17. converting primitive array to wrapper array
We can stream the array apply boxed and then convert to array for wrapper

int [] numbers={5,7,8,92,1,3};
Integer [] nums=Arrays.stream(numbers).boxed().toArray(Integer[]::new);
Integer [] nums=Arrays.stream(numbers).mapToObj(Integer::valueOf).toArray(Integer[]::new);
System.out.println(Arrays.toString(nums));

